ersation-ledger gained `package.json` exports + `gitUserIdentity` actor\n31\tstamping (note: full transcript rescans can duplicate pre-identity events\n32\tsince `actor.id` is part of the event-id hash).\n33\t\n34\tEnd-state decisions from 2026-07-21 (drive TODO priority):\n35\t- **Public npm release** is the goal — the `file:../conversation-ledger` dep\n36\t  must become a published semver dep before turnbridge can publish.\n37\t- **Embrace cledger 0.8.0 auto-re-anchor** (readEvents now may write re_anchor\n38\t  events + print stderr as a side effect): keep it on for lineage-survives-\n39\t  rebase; turnbridge just keeps the stderr noise out of its picker UI.\n40\t- **Verify interactive resume paths now** — all fabrication verification was\n41\t  headless (`-p` / `codex exec`); interactive resume for both CLIs was never\n42\t  content-confirmed.\n43\t- **Deepen Claude Code ⇄ Codex** rather than adding a third CLI target\n44\t  (though the user expects both deepening and broadening before release).\n45\t- npm publish of both packages deliberately deferred for a few days of\n46\t  dogfooding; turnbridge's `prepublishOnly` refuses while the ledger dep is\n47\t  `file:`. Both npm names were unclaimed as of 2026-07-21.\n48\t- Drift-agent stage 2 (CI agent drafts revalidation PRs) deferred — the\n49\t  commented-out job lives in `.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`.\n50\t- As of 2026-07-21: interactive resume verified on both CLIs via\n51\t  `npm run smoke:interactive` (expect-based pty; macOS `script` can't run\n52\t  ptyless) + `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs`; codex 0.145 validated\n53\t  (prefix list); 61 tests; ledger reads sequenced + stderr-buffered.\n54\t\n55\tTwo non-obvious findings from the 2026-07-19 follow-up session:\n56\t- **Codex TUI scrollback renders from `event_msg` records, not `response_item`.**\n57\t  The model still SEES history from response_items (user confirmed resumed\n58\t  Codex knew the prior context), but the screen looks empty without event_msg\n59\t  `user_message`/`agent_message` twins. Codex fabrication now emits both;\n60\t  shapes byte-match real rollout files.\n61\t- **Bridging is a fork, not a move.** Fabricating a target session → target CLI\n62\t  captures it as a NEW conversation under the id turnbridge generated (Codex\n63\t  resume preserves the v4 id and appends). So both source and target show in\n64\t  the picker — a real branch. Turnbridge records a `continuation` ledger event\n65\t  (kind `continuation`, `links` rel `continues`, content `imported_through_seq`)\n66\t  at fabricate time; picker labels lineage both directions and warns on\n67\t  re-bridge. Default shows BOTH endpoints (no abandonment assumed). That edge\n68\t  is also intent-recall's dedup key for the copied prefix. Related: [[evintunador-workflow-preferences]].\n69\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VzQZ8Ljrq1hMLVe1DNEQqm","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","dirty_fingerprint":"cf8b9e3c1e47cd671f179e23127d98edb70689fbf4ed08f9960baec974f11cfc","head":"e93df4508cf4d0567748cc27a493b0ff9b19ef36","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","seq":711},"id":"ev1-b9f16a6517becd1d5e9c80cd3f407fecfdbc225efdeb24f5b7d313ac8ef61a04","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T02:50:28.647Z","producer":{"session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix/opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 13 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Veri