{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Yes — cledger `0.18.0` on `main` has it (PR #2 merged), and turnbridge already resolves to it through the `file:` symlink, so it was live without a reinstall.\n\nI verified the newly-unlocked directions rather than just documenting them, and the round trip turned out to be a neat closed loop: `turnbridge list` now shows an **OpenCode** row that is one of my own fabricated test sessions, captured back by the `session.idle` plugin. Bridging it onward:\n\n- **opencode → Codex** — tool call replayed as a structured `function_call`/`function_call_output` pair, original `call_id` (`toolu_01abc`) and name (`Read`) intact.\n- **opencode → Claude Code** — same call as `tool_use`/`tool_result`, with `claude-opus-5` preserved as the assistant model id.\n- **opencode → opencode** — takes the native path (`opencode -s <id>`), no fabrication.\n\nSo the model id I propagate on fabrication survives a full Claude Code → opencode → ledger → Codex loop. Both fabricated test files are deleted.\n\nDocs updated and pushed (`e93df45`): the \"target only\" caveat is gone from the README, the design doc's status line is now `Claude Code ⇄ Codex ⇄ opencode`, and the main-flow step notes opencode is captured via the plugin rather than a tailed transcript. Two asymmetries recorded so they don't get rediscovered the hard way:\n\n- **opencode reasoning is plaintext**, so it arrives as ordinary visible `thinking` blocks — nothing provider-private is replayed for this target, unlike the Codex⇄Codex encrypted-reasoning path.\n- **Capture skips unsettled (`running`) tool calls**, so a bridged session only ever carries completed ones. That's *why* this round trip was lossless, and it wouldn't necessarily be for a session captured mid-tool-call.\n\nI also marked the \"deepen two CLIs rather than add a third\" decision as superseded in memory, since that's now the opposite of where the project landed.\n\nOne thing I left alone